      en: "Kandava Historical Stone Bridge spans the Abava River in Kandava. Built in 1803, it is one of Latvia's oldest surviving stone bridges. It features three arches made of local dolomite stone. Repaired multiple times, it retains its original appearance. Today it is closed to vehicles and serves as a pedestrian bridge. It is a national cultural monument and a popular photo spot, symbolizing the historic trade route through Courland.",
