      en: "Nīca, located in western Latvia, is a cultural hub known for its traditional crafts and history. The settlement dates back to the 13th century, with its first written mention in 1253. Nīca is famous for its unique embroidery style, which was added to the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2018. The village features wooden architecture from the 19th century, including the Nīca Community House built in 1882. Local folklore and song traditions remain vibrant.",
